# New Project Workflow

## Objective

Start every new project with a consistent AI context, documentation contracts,
and ChatGPT export support.

## Checklist

1.  Select the appropriate project profile from `core/project-profiles/` and
    create/scaffold the project. Choose the stack intentionally; once
    scaffolded, treat the installed environment as the starting point.
2.  Bootstrap AI Platform infrastructure into the project:
    - Preferred: from the project root, run `bootstrap-ai` (or
      `scripts/bootstrap-project.sh` with the project path).
    - Fallback: run `scripts/bootstrap-project.sh` from the AI Platform
      repository and supply the target path when prompted.
3.  Establish project-specific documentation contracts **before** substantive
    feature development. Bootstrap installs templates and shared
    infrastructure only; it does not populate project truth.
4.  Export initial ChatGPT context and upload to your ChatGPT Project.
5.  Begin implementation.

## Bootstrap Target Resolution

`scripts/bootstrap-project.sh` resolves the target project as follows:

1. Explicit path argument, if supplied
2. Current working directory (`$PWD`) when invoked from outside the AI
   Platform repository
3. Interactive prompt as the fallback

## Bootstrap Provides

Running bootstrap on a target project:

-   Links shared Cursor rules into `.cursor/rules/`
-   Links `scripts/export-chatgpt-context.sh`
-   Copies documentation templates when `docs/README.md` does not exist
-   Adds `.build/` to `.gitignore` when missing
-   Restores required project skills

Bootstrap is safe to re-run on an already-bootstrapped project.

## Post-Bootstrap: Establish Project Context

After bootstrap, an agent (or human) must inspect the **actual** project and
establish or update project-specific documentation contracts:

1. Inspect the existing project structure, installed environment,
   dependencies, architecture, and any available documentation.
2. Fill or update `docs/00-project-context.md` and foundational contracts so
   they describe this project — not generic platform assumptions or leftover
   template placeholders.
3. Follow Current-First Engineering in `00-platform`:
   - Existing projects: installed environment is the starting point.
   - Newly scaffolded projects: respect the selected/installed stack.
   - Do not upgrade dependencies merely because newer versions exist;
     upgrades require explicit direction or approval under platform Safety
     rules.

Do not begin substantive feature work while project contracts still contain
only unfilled template placeholders.

## Initial Documentation Contracts

Every project must include:

-   `docs/README.md` — dependency graph and contract registry
-   `docs/00-project-context.md` — concise ChatGPT and agent entry point
-   `docs/99-project-status.md` — current implementation status (update when
    phases or major milestones complete)

Minimum viable contracts:

-   `docs/contracts/foundational/vision.md`
-   `docs/contracts/foundational/architecture.md`

Add engine and feature contracts as the project grows. Do not create the
legacy four-file layout for new projects.

## ChatGPT Export

After customizing documentation:

```bash
scripts/export-chatgpt-context.sh
```

Upload `.build/chatgpt-context.zip` to the ChatGPT Project. Re-export when
documentation, Cursor rules, agent skills, or AI metadata change.

## Maintenance

All contracts must be maintained in accordance with the `10-documentation`
project rule.
